{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Cinematic Bullet-Hit Compositing.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Cinematic Bullet-Hit Compositing.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"cinematic bullet hit compositing cinematic bullet hit compositing","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Cinematic Bullet-Hit Compositing.md","fileName":"Cinematic Bullet-Hit Compositing.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Cinematic Bullet-Hit Compositing","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-15 18:17\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Particle and Destruction VFX]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Particle and Destruction VFX","Interactive Light from Muzzle Flashes","digitalvisualeffectsandcompositing.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Cinematic Bullet-Hit Compositing.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Cinematic Bullet-Hit Compositing.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"cinematic bullet hit compositing cinematic bullet hit compositing","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Cinematic Bullet-Hit Compositing.md","fileName":"Cinematic Bullet-Hit Compositing.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Cinematic Bullet-Hit Compositing","heading":"Cinematic Bullet-Hit Compositing","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"A screen bullet hit follows the visual convention and tone of the production, which may differ from a literal entry wound. The book times a desaturated, darkened burst to the performer's reaction and places a second elongated burst behind the body for an exit effect, using roto to prevent the rear element from crossing in front. A still spray image on a perspective-aligned card can be revealed with a moving soft matte. The composite is built from timed layers rather than one footage overlay. See [[Interactive Light from Muzzle Flashes]] for the related gunfire cue.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Particl